        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/9f8e36/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-06T20:37:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I’ve seen a lot of answers to at the end of turn-  so in effect when a card at the end of turn causes another card to be played that says at the end of turn the subsequent end of turn card also has its effect before the turn is over. But my question is that I can’t seem to find the answer to is if a card that reads at the start of turn causes another at the start of turn card to be drawn - does that card play that turn or does it wait to have it at the start of turn effect till the next turn? I appreciate the help!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:53.119Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
