      {
        "id": 164918,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-06T20:44:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The short answer is yes. &nbsp;Start of turn effects that are played during start of turn trigger the same way that end of turn effects trigger when played at end of turn.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The longer answer is that start of turn effects and end of turn effects always trigger in the order that the cards came into play. &nbsp;So the Villain character card is always first, and then whatever was played next, then the one after that, etc. &nbsp;Since a just played card by definition came into play after the card that caused it to be played, it will still be in line to be triggered.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:46:12.839Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
