      {
        "id": 164920,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-07T01:04:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Since the order for start and end of turn effects are the order they enter play, it works.</p><p>Basically you do the following:</p><p>Start of turn: &nbsp;Check for start of turn effects that haven't already been activated this turn, if there are any resolve the first one that entered play, then repeat. &nbsp;Continue until all start of turn effects have been activated.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Do the same for the end of turn effects.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:46:12.977Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
